  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "實習法庭(二)",
    "sub_ename": "MOOT COURT(2)",
    "describe_ch": "如何進一步搜索法學資料、撰寫訴訟文書、和進行口頭辯論，學生將被要求就實際案例模擬法庭運作情形。 課程著重在訴訟文書撰寫的技巧和法庭上交互詰問的模擬，希望加強同學對司法體系運作情形的認識。",
    "describe_eh": "The Moot Court class teaches students the fundamentals of complex legal research, persuasive legal writing, and effective oral argument. Moot Court topics are chosen from real cases. Students will research and write an appellate brief on behalf of one of the parties and then perform a formal oral argument before a panel of judges. The course emphasizes effective research and writing techniques and introduces the students to making oral arguments in court.",
